:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME=VALEML.Validate an Email Address
:P.This command is used to validate an email address. It accepts
an email address field and returns an F in the PASS field if it
is not valid. The command is intended to be used in CL programs
to make validating emails easier and require less coding.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='VALEML/EMAIL'.CL Email Address Variable
:P.:HP2.EMAIL:EHP2.
Specifies the CL variable that contains the email address to be validated.
:p.This is a required parameter.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='VALEML/PASS'.The Return Variable
:P.:HP2.PASS:EHP2. The variable name to receive the email status.
:P.The command will return an F in this variable if the email s
address is not valid. The variable has to be defined a *CHAR Len(1).
to promote programmer familiarity the variable name should be
PASS.
:p.This is a required parameter.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:EPNLGRP.
